  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "Using the high-resolution GRID3 dataset, this study applied Kernel Density Estimation, Nearest Neighbor Distance, and Ripley's K and L functions to evaluate settlement patterns across Ghana. The analysis revealed high-density settlement hotspots concentrated in southern regions such as Greater Accra, Ashanti, Central, Eastern, and Western, contrasted with dispersed, lower-density patterns across the northern savannah regions. Spatial clustering was confirmed to be statistically significant across multiple spatial scales in the south.",
      "why": "It quantifies the national-scale disparity between the compact, highly aggregated urban clusters in southern Ghana and the dispersed settlement structures in the north, providing an empirical baseline for regional infrastructure and emergency service planning."
    }
